        question: "What is the difference between a Video Editor and a Motion Graphics Designer?",
        answers: ["Both roles may collaborate, but their primary ownership is different:", "<strong>Video Editor - Post-Production Owner:</strong> Structures footage, controls pacing, selects takes and B-roll, cleans audio, applies color corrections, adds approved graphics, manages revisions, and prepares final platform-specific exports.", "<strong>Motion Graphics Designer - Animation Specialist:</strong> Focuses more deeply on animated typography, 2D or 3D graphics, compositing, explainers, motion systems, product animation, and advanced visual effects. Some editors combine both skill sets, but the required depth should be defined before hiring."]
    },
