                title="The U.S. Video Production Challenge: Rising Costs and Fragmented Post-Production"
                highlightWord="Video Production"
                description="Many U.S. companies produce more footage than their internal marketing teams can edit consistently. Social clips, webinar recordings, product demos, founder videos, podcasts, customer stories, and paid-media variations accumulate in shared drives while publishing deadlines continue to move. When editing is distributed across marketers, contractors, and agencies, brand consistency and turnaround become harder to control. <br><br>For U.S. teams hiring video editor talent locally, dedicated capacity can solve the ownership problem, but it also adds recruiting time, payroll administration, benefits, software, equipment planning, management overhead, and replacement risk. Agencies can provide broad creative support, yet every new cutdown, revision, or format may depend on scope and account-team availability. Freelancers can be effective for defined projects, but recurring volume may be difficult to plan when their time is divided across clients."
