                imageAlt="Editor de video remoto trabajando en postproducción"
                badgeText="High-Impact Post-Production"
                quoteText=""
                checklistTitle="Scaling video production in the United States often creates three recurring operational pressures:"
                checklistItems={[
                    "<strong>Local Payroll Overhead:</strong> An in-house W-2 video editor requires more than base compensation: recruiting, payroll taxes, benefits, software, hardware, management time, and replacement costs all affect the total employment budget. Each video editor hire also carries onboarding, workflow documentation, and replacement considerations.",
                    "<strong>Agency Scope Fragmentation:</strong> Agency retainers and project packages can work well for campaigns, but recurring revisions, cutdowns, subtitles, platform versions, and source-file requests may depend on the exact statement of work. Some companies therefore outsource video editing to create more predictable recurring post-production capacity.",
                    "<strong>Freelance Capacity Gaps:</strong> A freelance video editor may be ideal for isolated projects, but availability, response time, file organization, and brand familiarity can vary when the professional is balancing several clients. Teams that hire freelance video editor support should compare availability, revision ownership, source-file handoff, and long-term continuity before choosing a model.",
